# Git push policy

Whenever this project has local modifications that should be kept (docs, code, shortcut builds, etc.):

1. Commit with a clear message (author: `tobiieyetracker` / `tobiieyetracker@users.noreply.github.com` via `git -c`, do not change global git config).
2. Push to `origin` (`main`) immediately after the commit.
3. Do not wait for the user to ask again to push — they requested continuous push for local changes.
